        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1065">

                <pb facs="0788" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3286</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Canada.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On April 22 Department endeavored to despatch three telegrams to Consul at
                    Frontera but informed by telegraph office that telegrams had been stopped by
                    Mexican Government censor at Coatza-coalcos. Endeavor to communicate in some way
                    with Frontera and instruct Consul there to provide all Americans with passage
                    who may require assistance, using his judgment as to routing them via New
                    Orleans or Galveston.</p>
                <p>Also endeavor to communicate with Ciudad del Carmen, Campeche, and inform
                    Woodruff and family that relatives urge them to leave Mexico at once. Also
                    inform W. M. Ferris at Carmen, who is manager of Hearst properties in Campeche,
                    that it is the desire of Edward H. Clark that Ferris and other American
                    employees leave Mexico as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>If practicable it may be advisable to send light draft boat to places
                    mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
